  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing (NAICS 325412) has $113M in obligations in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 99.3% year over year. The market produced 817 awards so far, with an average award size of $139K. FY2027 totals are partial because the fiscal year is not complete. Fiscal history shows large swings: FY22 obligations were $34.4B, then moved to $12.8B in FY23, $10.1B in FY24, $13.1B in FY25, and $16B in FY26. The top buyers so far are the Department of Veterans Affairs with $79.5M and the Department of Justice with $32.3M. The largest vendors so far are MCKESSON CORPORATION with $31.9M, CARDINAL HEALTH 414, LLC with $15.4M, and PROGENICS PHARMACEUTICALS INC with $14.8M. The data show a concentrated buyer base and a heavy drop in obligations compared with the prior year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What happened to obligations in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing obligations fell 99.3% year over year. FY2027 to date obligations total $113M, a sharp fall from prior fiscal years that topped $34.4B in FY22 and ranged between $10.1B and $16B from FY23 to FY26. The current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is not complete."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main buyers and vendors so far in FY2027?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs and the Department of Justice are the dominant buyers, with $79.5M and $32.3M respectively. MCKESSON CORPORATION, CARDINAL HEALTH 414, LLC, and PROGENICS PHARMACEUTICALS INC are the largest vendors, with $31.9M, $15.4M, and $14.8M respectively. Several agencies show minimal or zero obligations in this period, keeping spending concentrated."
      }
    ]
  },
